  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**La voz pasiva simple**",
      "",
      "| Tiempo | Estructura | Ejemplo |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| **Presente** | *am / is / are + participio* | *Phones **are made** in Asia.* |",
      "| **Pasado** | *was / were + participio* | *The first phone **was invented** in 1992.* |",
      "",
      "**¿Cuándo se usa?**",
      "",
      "- Cuando **no sabemos** quién hace la acción: *My bike was stolen.*",
      "- Cuando **no importa**: *The room is cleaned every day.*",
      "- Cuando el **objeto** es lo importante: *The phones are shipped all over the world.*",
      "",
      "**Active → Passive**",
      "",
      "- *Workers **make** the phones.* → *The phones **are made** (by workers).*",
      "- *Edison **invented** the bulb.* → *The bulb **was invented** by Edison.*",
      "",
      "**Negativa e interrogativa**",
      "",
      "- *The phone **isn't** made here.* · *The phones **weren't** sold in 1990.*",
      "- ***Is** it made here?* · ***Were** they sold in 1990?*",
      "",
      "**Participios irregulares útiles:** *make → made · build → built · write → written · sell → sold · take → taken · find → found · steal → stolen · do → done · see → seen · know → known.*",
      "",
      "**Ojo:** en español usamos 'se' (se fabrica). En inglés: ***is made*** (nunca *it makes*). Y el participio no cambia con el sujeto: *The phone **was** made / The phones **were** made.*",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *manufactured* /ˌmænjuˈfæktʃəd/ · *assembled* /əˈsembld/ · *invented* /ɪnˈventɪd/."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "The phone make in China.",
        "right": "The phone is made in China.",
        "note": "Pasiva = be + participio."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "It was steal.",
        "right": "It was stolen.",
        "note": "Participio irregular."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
